NOTICE — apollo11-agc-study
==========================

This repository is a study / convenience workspace that aggregates guides and
pointers to upstream Apollo Guidance Computer (AGC) materials.

What this repo claims
---------------------
- Documentation under docs/ and the top-level README.md were written for this
  repository (apollo11-agc-study). They are study notes, not NASA or MIT
  publications.

What this repo does NOT claim
-----------------------------
- Ownership of NASA / MIT Instrumentation Laboratory Apollo flight software.
- Ownership of Virtual AGC tools, webAGC, or other upstream projects.

Upstream flight software (Public Domain)
----------------------------------------
- Source tree via submodule: flight-software/Apollo-11
  Upstream: https://github.com/chrislgarry/Apollo-11
  Marked Public Domain Mark 1.0 (see that repo's LICENSE.md).
- Digitized from MIT Museum printouts; transcription work associated with the
  Virtual AGC project (http://www.ibiblio.org/apollo/).
- Corresponding AGC sources also appear inside tools/virtualagc (e.g.
  Comanche055/, Luminary099/) and are likewise treated as public domain by
  upstream.

Upstream tools (GPL and other)
------------------------------
- tools/virtualagc — https://github.com/virtualagc/virtualagc
  Bulk of Virtual AGC PC software: GNU GPL version 2 or later (see COPYING /
  LICENSE.txt in that tree). Flight AGC/AGS software therein: public domain.
  Some portions may use less-restrictive licenses; see individual files.
- tools/webAGC — https://github.com/michaelfranzl/webAGC
  See that repository's LICENSE for terms of the browser emulator / demo.

Submodules
----------
Flight software and tools are included as git submodules so licensing and
attribution remain with upstream. Prefer cloning with:

  git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/huming0618/apollo11-agc-study.git

Do not treat this study repo as a re-license or re-publication of NASA/MIT code.
